      "message": "Ignores Wi-Fi validation failures after roam.\n\nIf validation fails on a Wi-Fi network after a roam to a new BSSID, assume that the roam temporarily disrupted network connectivity, and ignore all failures until this time has passed. NetworkMonitor will continue to attempt validation, and if it fails after this time has passed, the network will be marked unvalidated.\n\nOnly supported up to S. On T+, the Wi-Fi code should use destroyAndAwaitReplacement in order to ensure that apps see the network disconnect and reconnect.",
